==Aftermath==
===Accusations of electoral fraud===
The opposition has decided to contest the result; [[Mircea Geoană]] announced that the Social Democrats will contest the elections at the Constitutional Court and will submit evidence of electoral fraud.<ref name="hotnews.ro">{{Cite web|url=https://english.hotnews.ro/stiri-top_news-6691428-social-democrats-decided-contest-elections-mircea-geoana-exclude-any-collaboration-with-the-democrat-liberals-and-maintain-the-majority-with-the-liberals-and-hungarian-democrats.htm|title=Social Democrats decided to contest elections / Mircea Geoana: we exclude any collaboration with the Democrat Liberals and maintain the majority with the Liberals and Hungarian Democrats – Top News – HotNews.ro|date=7 December 2009|website=english.hotnews.ro}}</ref> PSD Secretary General [[Liviu Dragnea]] cited "a high number of void ballots, modified voting protocols, and massive electoral tourism".<ref name="SofiaEcho" /> [[Liviu Dragnea|Dragnea]] stated: "Romanians voted for Mircea Geoană, but Băsescu's state apparatus is trying to make him the presidential winner through fraud".<ref name="yahoonews">{{Cite web|url=http://ca.news.yahoo.com/s/capress/091207/world/eu_romania_presidential_elections|title=Romania opposition party contests election results, accusing Basescu supporters of fraud|access-date=7 December 2009|archive-date=30 January 2010|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100130034804/http://ca.news.yahoo.com/s/capress/091207/world/eu_romania_presidential_elections|url-status=dead}}</ref> Former Prime Minister [[Adrian Năstase]] and former President [[Ion Iliescu]], both PSD members, also stated that they doubted the results.{{citation needed|date=June 2012}}

Mircea Geoană has also stated that the Social Democrats exclude any collaboration with Băsescu and his party, and maintain the majority with the Liberals and Hungarian Democrats,<ref name="hotnews.ro" /> while Crin Antonescu also stated that the Liberal Party excludes "any participation in a Traian Băsescu puppet government".<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://english.hotnews.ro/stiri-politics-6706652-liberal-leader-crin-antonescu-basescu-does-not-wish-for-government-with-pnl-but-engulf-compromise-break-the-liberals.htm|title=Liberal leader Crin Antonescu: Basescu does not wish for a Government with PNL, but to engulf, compromise or break the liberals – Politics – HotNews.ro|date=10 December 2009|website=english.hotnews.ro}}</ref>

===Constitutional Court proceedings===
On 8 December, the Social Democratic Party submitted their request to annul and repeat the presidential election run-off to the Constitutional Court, saying the election was rigged.<ref name="romaniantimes.at"/>

On 11 December, in an unprecedented decision the Constitutional Court decided to recount all 138,476 invalid votes.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.antena3.ro/politica/curtea-constitutionala-a-decis-renumararea-voturilor-nule-87209.html|title=Curtea Constituţională a decis renumărarea voturilor nule|website=www.antena3.ro}}</ref> After 137,613 invalid votes recounted, only 2,137 were revalidated (1.6% of recounted invalid votes), 1,169 votes for Traian Băsescu and 968 for Mircea Geoană.<ref>{{in lang|ro}} [http://www.impactnews.ro/Alegeri/S-a-%C3%AEncheiat-renum%C4%83rarea-voturilor-na%C5%A3ionale-nule-de-la-BEC-25535 S-a încheiat renumărarea voturilor naţionale nule de la BEC] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091215141643/http://www.impactnews.ro/Alegeri/S-a-%C3%AEncheiat-renum%C4%83rarea-voturilor-na%C5%A3ionale-nule-de-la-BEC-25535 |date=15 December 2009 }}</ref>

On 14 December, the Constitutional Court rejected the request to repeat the presidential elections, paving the way to validate Băsescu's election.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.antena3.ro/politica/alegerile-nu-se-repeta-cererea-psd-de-anulare-a-turului-ii-respinsa-de-ccr-basescu-obtine-un-nou-87411.html|title=Alegerile nu se repetă: Cererea PSD de anulare a turului II, respinsă de CCR. Băsescu obţine un nou mandat|website=www.antena3.ro}}</ref> The same day, Geoană admitted defeat and wished Băsescu good luck in his second term in office.<ref>{{in lang|ro}} [http://prezidentiale.evz.ro/emain/articolul/879745/Geoana-Ii-urez-succes-lui-Traian-Basescu- Geoană: Îi urez succes lui Traian Băsescu!] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091217091127/http://prezidentiale.evz.ro/emain/articolul/879745/Geoana-Ii-urez-succes-lui-Traian-Basescu- |date=17 December 2009 }}</ref>

